  "reasoning": "According to the Congressional Research Service (CRS) and historical budget records, the last time Congress enacted all regular annual appropriations bills before the start of the fiscal year (October 1) was for Fiscal Year 1997 (completed in late September 1996). Since the modern congressional budget process was established under the Congressional Budget and Impoundment Control Act of 1974, all regular spending bills have been passed on time in only four fiscal years: FY 1977, FY 1989, FY 1995, and FY 1997. Since then, Congress has consistently relied on continuing resolutions and late omnibus spending packages to fund the federal government.",
